{"level":30,"time":1778514165580,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DNk5YP37toAEt38cYknqXM","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Conductor\n     2→\n     3→YAML-based workflow orchestration engine that runs inside Vercel Sandboxes and executes workflows from Bureau.\n     4→\n     5→## Local Development Setup\n     6→\n     7→Before running workflows locally:\n     8→\n     9→1. **Install dependencies**\n    10→   ```bash\n    11→   npm install\n    12→   ```\n    13→\n    14→2. **Create workspace folder**\n    15→   ```bash\n    16→   mkdir workspace\n    17→   ```\n    18→   This folder is gitignored and will contain all workflow artifacts.\n    19→\n    20→3. **Symlink Bureau into workspace**\n    21→   ```bash\n    22→   ln -s /path/to/bureau workspace/bureau\n    23→   ```\n    24→   Replace `/path/to/bureau` with your local bureau repo path.\n    25→\n    26→4. **Configure environment**\n    27→   ```bash\n    28→   cp .env.example .env\n    29→   ```\n    30→   Fill in values from 1Password or get from a team member.\n    31→\n    32→5. **Run smoke test to verify setup**\n    33→   ```bash\n    34→   npm run conduct -- --workflow=smoke-test --jurisdiction=austin --department-code=de --site-plan-id=f98d6cc3-d49b-4108-87ab-3ca457418d2e\n    35→   ```\n    36→   This runs a minimal test workflow to verify your configuration.\n    37→\n    38→6. **Verify upload in Supabase**\n    39→\n    40→   Check Supabase storage at `workflow-runs/smoke-test` to confirm the upload succeeded.\n    41→\n    42→## Overview\n    43→\n    44→Conductor manages step execution, parallel agent coordination, retries, and resume capability for agentic workflows like site plan reviews and training.\n    45→\n    46→```\n    47→Dispatcher (Vercel + Inngest)\n    48→    ↓ creates sandbox, passes workflow name + inputs\n    49→Conductor (Sandbox)\n    50→    ↓ clones Bureau, loads workflow.yaml\n    51→    ↓ executes steps sequentially\n    52→    ↓ fires completion webhook\n    53→Bureau (Git Repo)\n    54→    └── workflows, prompts, regulatory codes\n    55→```\n    56→\n    57→## Key Features\n    58→\n    59→- **Parallel execution**: Steps with checklists run agents in parallel (up to `maxWorkers`)\n    60→- **Retry & resume**: Per-step retries with exponential backoff, state persists to `status.json`\n    61→- **Resource preparation**: Clones Bureau, downloads site plan files, sets up workspace\n    62→- **Agent runner**: Wraps Claude Agent SDK with MCP tools (vision, progress)\n    63→\n    64→## CLI Usage\n    65→\n    66→```bash\n    67→# Smoke test (run first to verify setup)\n    68→npm run conduct -- --workflow=smoke-test --jurisdiction=austin --department-code=de --site-plan-id=f98d6cc3-d49b-4108-87ab-3ca457418d2e\n    69→\n    70→# Run a review\n    71→npm run conduct -- --workflow=review-3.0.1 --jurisdiction=austin --department-code=de --eval --site-plan-id=f98d6cc3-d49b-4108-87ab-3ca457418d2e\n    72→\n    73→# Run a completeness check\n    74→npm run conduct -- --workflow=completeness-check --site-plan-id=<uuid>\n    75→\n    76→# Run a training\n    77→npm run conduct -- --workflow=train-3.1 --department-code=de --jurisdiction=austin\n    78→\n    79→# Resume an interrupted workflow\n    80→npm run conduct -- --resume\n    81→\n    82→# Resume and also retry failed items\n    83→npm run conduct -- --resume --reset-failed\n    84→```\n    85→\n    86→## Recovering from a Failed Run\n    87→\n    88→If a workflow fails or is interrupted (e.g., ran out of API credits, process killed):\n    89→\n    90→1. **Check workflow state**\n    91→\n    92→   Open `workspace/workflow/status.json` to see the current state:\n    93→   - `status`: `\"error\"` or `\"in-progress\"` indicates incomplete workflow\n    94→   - `step` / `stepName`: Which step was running when it stopped\n    95→   - `checklist`: Array of items with their statuses (`queued`, `in-progress`, `done`, `failed`)\n    96→\n    97→2. **Reset stuck items**\n    98→\n    99→   Before resuming, reset any items stuck in `in-progress` or `failed` state. Edit `status.json`:\n   100→   - Change `status` from `\"error\"` to `\"in-progress\"`\n   101→   - In the `checklist` array, change any items with `\"status\": \"in-progress\"` or `\"status\": \"failed\"` back to `\"status\": \"queued\"`\n   102→   - Remove `error`, `startedAt`, and `endedAt` fields from reset items\n   103→\n   104→3. **Resume the workflow**\n   105→   ```bash\n   106→   npm run conduct -- --resume\n   107→   ```\n   108→   This automatically resets `in-progress` items and continues from where it left off.\n   109→\n   110→   To also retry failed items:\n   111→   ```bash\n   112→   npm run conduct -- --resume --reset-failed\n   113→   ```\n   114→\n   115→**Example status.json before recovery:**\n   116→```json\n   117→{\n   118→  \"status\": \"error\",\n   119→  \"workflow\": \"review-3.0.1\",\n   120→  \"step\": 2,\n   121→  \"stepName\": \"review-codes\",\n   122→  \"checklist\": [\n   123→    { \"value\": \"01\", \"status\": \"done\", \"index\": 1 },\n   124→    { \"value\": \"02\", \"status\": \"in-progress\", \"index\": 2, \"startedAt\": \"...\" },\n   125→    { \"value\": \"03\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"index\": 3, \"error\": \"...\" },\n   126→    { \"value\": \"04\", \"status\": \"queued\", \"index\": 4 }\n   127→  ]\n   128→}\n   129→```\n   130→\n   131→**After running `--resume --reset-failed`:**\n   132→- Items 02 and 03 are reset to `queued` and will be retried\n   133→- Workflow continues from step 2\n   134→\n   135→## Post-Workflow Checklist\n   136→\n   137→After any workflow run completes:\n   138→\n   139→1. **Verify upload to Supabase storage**\n   140→\n   141→   Check `workflow-runs/{workflow-name}` in Supabase storage to confirm outputs uploaded successfully.\n   142→\n   143→2. **Clean workspace**\n   144→\n   145→   Delete everything in `workspace/` except the `bureau` symlink:\n   146→   ```bash\n   147→   # From conductor directory\n   148→   find workspace -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 ! -name 'bureau' -exec rm -rf {} +\n   149→   ```\n   150→\n   151→## Using Training Output\n   152→\n   153→After a training workflow completes successfully:\n   154→\n   155→1. **Locate training output**\n   156→\n   157→   Find the output in `workspace/output/formal-review/`\n   158→\n   159→2. **Copy to Bureau**\n   160→\n   161→   Copy the output to the appropriate department in Bureau:\n   162→   ```bash\n   163→   cp -r workspace/output/formal-review/* /path/to/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/departments/{deptCode}/formal-review/\n   164→   ```\n   165→   If a `formal-review` folder already exists, delete it first and copy in the new one.\n   166→\n   167→3. **Commit and merge to Bureau**\n   168→\n   169→   Create a PR to merge the new training output to Bureau's main branch.\n   170→\n   171→4. **Use in future reviews**\n   172→\n   173→   Once merged to Bureau main, future reviews will automatically use the new training output.\n   174→\n   175→## Directory Structure\n   176→\n   177→```\n   178→conductor/\n   179→├── src/\n   180→│   ├── index.ts                    # CLI entry point\n   181→│   ├── orchestrator/\n   182→│   │   ├── engine.ts               # Core orchestration engine\n   183→│   │   ├── workflow-loader.ts      # YAML config loader & validator\n   184→│   │   ├── step-executor.ts        # Single & parallel step execution\n   185→│   │   ├── checklist-manager.ts    # Atomic checklist operations\n   186→│   │   ├── template-engine.ts      # {{ variable }} renderer\n   187→│   │   ├── resource-manager.ts     # Workspace resource setup\n   188→│   │   └── types.ts                # TypeScript interfaces\n   189→│   ├── agent/\n   190→│   │   └── runner.ts               # Agent SDK wrapper\n   191→│   ├── tools/\n   192→│   │   ├── progress.ts             # Progress MCP tool\n   193→│   │   ├── vision.ts               # Vision MCP tool\n   194→│   │   └── index.ts                # Tool registry\n   195→│   └── shared/\n   196→│       ├── logger.ts               # Pino + Betterstack\n   197→│       ├── webhook.ts              # Webhook sender\n   198→│       ├── supabase.ts             # Supabase client\n   199→│       ├── git.ts                  # Git operations\n   200→│       └── github.ts               # GitHub PR creation\n   201→└── package.json\n   202→```\n   203→\n   204→## Workspace Structure\n   205→\n   206→At runtime, conductor creates a predictable workspace:\n   207→```\n   208→workspace/\n   209→├── workflow/              # Copied from Bureau at startup\n   210→│   ├── workflow.yaml\n   211→│   ├── status.json        # Execution state tracking\n   212→│   └── prompts/\n   213→├── bureau/                # Cloned if resources.bureau: true\n   214→├── site-plans/{id}/       # Downloaded if resources.sitePlan defined\n   215→├── output/                # All workflow outputs\n   216→└── logs/                  # All workflow logs\n   217→```\n   218→\n   219→## Workflow Definition\n   220→\n   221→Workflows are defined in Bureau at `jurisdictions/{jurisdiction}/workflows/{name}/workflow.yaml`. See the architecture skill in the controlroom workspace for complete YAML schema documentation.\n   222→\n   223→## Environment Variables\n   224→\n   225→Required environment variables depend on the workflow. Common ones include:\n   226→- `WORKSPACE_PATH` - Base path for workspace directory\n   227→- `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` - Authentication for Claude agents\n   228→- `BETTERSTACK_HOST` / `BETTERSTACK_TOKEN` - Logging\n   229→- `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` / `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` - Database access\n   230→\n   231→## Related Documentation\n   232→\n   233→For comprehensive architecture and workflow YAML reference, see the architecture skill in the controlroom workspace (`controlroom/.claude/skills/architecture/`).\n   234→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02f3e714-877a-4005-af51-2af8f544a8d6","uuid":"1017afad-ba04-4d9d-9089-51e76250a824","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/README.md","content":"# Conductor\n\nYAML-based workflow orchestration engine that runs inside Vercel Sandboxes and executes workflows from Bureau.\n\n## Local Development Setup\n\nBefore running workflows locally:\n\n1. **Install dependencies**\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n\n2. **Create workspace folder**\n   ```bash\n   mkdir workspace\n   ```\n   This folder is gitignored and will contain all workflow artifacts.\n\n3. **Symlink Bureau into workspace**\n   ```bash\n   ln -s /path/to/bureau workspace/bureau\n   ```\n   Replace `/path/to/bureau` with your local bureau repo path.\n\n4. **Configure environment**\n   ```bash\n   cp .env.example .env\n   ```\n   Fill in values from 1Password or get from a team member.\n\n5. **Run smoke test to verify setup**\n   ```bash\n   npm run conduct -- --workflow=smoke-test --jurisdiction=austin --department-code=de --site-plan-id=f98d6cc3-d49b-4108-87ab-3ca457418d2e\n   ```\n   This runs a minimal test workflow to verify your configuration.\n\n6. **Verify upload in Supabase**\n\n   Check Supabase storage at `workflow-runs/smoke-test` to confirm the upload succeeded.\n\n## Overview\n\nConductor manages step execution, parallel agent coordination, retries, and resume capability for agentic workflows like site plan reviews and training.\n\n```\nDispatcher (Vercel + Inngest)\n    ↓ creates sandbox, passes workflow name + inputs\nConductor (Sandbox)\n    ↓ clones Bureau, loads workflow.yaml\n    ↓ executes steps sequentially\n    ↓ fires completion webhook\nBureau (Git Repo)\n    └── workflows, prompts, regulatory codes\n```\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Parallel execution**: Steps with checklists run agents in parallel (up to `maxWorkers`)\n- **Retry & resume**: Per-step retries with exponential backoff, state persists to `status.json`\n- **Resource preparation**: Clones Bureau, downloads site plan files, sets up workspace\n- **Agent runner**: Wraps Claude Agent SDK with MCP tools (vision, progress)\n\n## CLI Usage\n\n```bash\n# Smoke test (run first to verify setup)\nnpm run conduct -- --workflow=smoke-test --jurisdiction=austin --department-code=de --site-plan-id=f98d6cc3-d49b-4108-87ab-3ca457418d2e\n\n# Run a review\nnpm run conduct -- --workflow=review-3.0.1 --jurisdiction=austin --department-code=de --eval --site-plan-id=f98d6cc3-d49b-4108-87ab-3ca457418d2e\n\n# Run a completeness check\nnpm run conduct -- --workflow=completeness-check --site-plan-id=<uuid>\n\n# Run a training\nnpm run conduct -- --workflow=train-3.1 --department-code=de --jurisdiction=austin\n\n# Resume an interrupted workflow\nnpm run conduct -- --resume\n\n# Resume and also retry failed items\nnpm run conduct -- --resume --reset-failed\n```\n\n## Recovering from a Failed Run\n\nIf a workflow fails or is interrupted (e.g., ran out of API credits, process killed):\n\n1. **Check workflow state**\n\n   Open `workspace/workflow/status.json` to see the current state:\n   - `status`: `\"error\"` or `\"in-progress\"` indicates incomplete workflow\n   - `step` / `stepName`: Which step was running when it stopped\n   - `checklist`: Array of items with their statuses (`queued`, `in-progress`, `done`, `failed`)\n\n2. **Reset stuck items**\n\n   Before resuming, reset any items stuck in `in-progress` or `failed` state. Edit `status.json`:\n   - Change `status` from `\"error\"` to `\"in-progress\"`\n   - In the `checklist` array, change any items with `\"status\": \"in-progress\"` or `\"status\": \"failed\"` back to `\"status\": \"queued\"`\n   - Remove `error`, `startedAt`, and `endedAt` fields from reset items\n\n3. **Resume the workflow**\n   ```bash\n   npm run conduct -- --resume\n   ```\n   This automatically resets `in-progress` items and continues from where it left off.\n\n   To also retry failed items:\n   ```bash\n   npm run conduct -- --resume --reset-failed\n   ```\n\n**Example status.json before recovery:**\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"error\",\n  \"workflow\": \"review-3.0.1\",\n  \"step\": 2,\n  \"stepName\": \"review-codes\",\n  \"checklist\": [\n    { \"value\": \"01\", \"status\": \"done\", \"index\": 1 },\n    { \"value\": \"02\", \"status\": \"in-progress\", \"index\": 2, \"startedAt\": \"...\" },\n    { \"value\": \"03\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"index\": 3, \"error\": \"...\" },\n    { \"value\": \"04\", \"status\": \"queued\", \"index\": 4 }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**After running `--resume --reset-failed`:**\n- Items 02 and 03 are reset to `queued` and will be retried\n- Workflow continues from step 2\n\n## Post-Workflow Checklist\n\nAfter any workflow run completes:\n\n1. **Verify upload to Supabase storage**\n\n   Check `workflow-runs/{workflow-name}` in Supabase storage to confirm outputs uploaded successfully.\n\n2. **Clean workspace**\n\n   Delete everything in `workspace/` except the `bureau` symlink:\n   ```bash\n   # From conductor directory\n   find workspace -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 ! -name 'bureau' -exec rm -rf {} +\n   ```\n\n## Using Training Output\n\nAfter a training workflow completes successfully:\n\n1. **Locate training output**\n\n   Find the output in `workspace/output/formal-review/`\n\n2. **Copy to Bureau**\n\n   Copy the output to the appropriate department in Bureau:\n   ```bash\n   cp -r workspace/output/formal-review/* /path/to/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/departments/{deptCode}/formal-review/\n   ```\n   If a `formal-review` folder already exists, delete it first and copy in the new one.\n\n3. **Commit and merge to Bureau**\n\n   Create a PR to merge the new training output to Bureau's main branch.\n\n4. **Use in future reviews**\n\n   Once merged to Bureau main, future reviews will automatically use the new training output.\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\nconductor/\n├── src/\n│   ├── index.ts                    # CLI entry point\n│   ├── orchestrator/\n│   │   ├── engine.ts               # Core orchestration engine\n│   │   ├── workflow-loader.ts      # YAML config loader & validator\n│   │   ├── step-executor.ts        # Single & parallel step execution\n│   │   ├── checklist-manager.ts    # Atomic checklist operations\n│   │   ├── template-engine.ts      # {{ variable }} renderer\n│   │   ├── resource-manager.ts     # Workspace resource setup\n│   │   └── types.ts                # TypeScript interfaces\n│   ├── agent/\n│   │   └── runner.ts               # Agent SDK wrapper\n│   ├── tools/\n│   │   ├── progress.ts             # Progress MCP tool\n│   │   ├── vision.ts               # Vision MCP tool\n│   │   └── index.ts                # Tool registry\n│   └── shared/\n│       ├── logger.ts               # Pino + Betterstack\n│       ├── webhook.ts              # Webhook sender\n│       ├── supabase.ts             # Supabase client\n│       ├── git.ts                  # Git operations\n│       └── github.ts               # GitHub PR creation\n└── package.json\n```\n\n## Workspace Structure\n\nAt runtime, conductor creates a predictable workspace:\n```\nworkspace/\n├── workflow/              # Copied from Bureau at startup\n│   ├── workflow.yaml\n│   ├── status.json        # Execution state tracking\n│   └── prompts/\n├── bureau/                # Cloned if resources.bureau: true\n├── site-plans/{id}/       # Downloaded if resources.sitePlan defined\n├── output/                # All workflow outputs\n└── logs/                  # All workflow logs\n```\n\n## Workflow Definition\n\nWorkflows are defined in Bureau at `jurisdictions/{jurisdiction}/workflows/{name}/workflow.yaml`. See the architecture skill in the controlroom workspace for complete YAML schema documentation.\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nRequired environment variables depend on the workflow. Common ones include:\n- `WORKSPACE_PATH` - Base path for workspace directory\n- `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` - Authentication for Claude agents\n- `BETTERSTACK_HOST` / `BETTERSTACK_TOKEN` - Logging\n- `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` / `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` - Database access\n\n## Related Documentation\n\nFor comprehensive architecture and workflow YAML reference, see the architecture skill in the controlroom workspace (`controlroom/.claude/skills/architecture/`).\n","numLines":234,"startLine":1,"totalLines":234}}}
