mine if transformers are proposed. In this case, I should mark items based on their applicability conditions:\n- Items marked \"All sites\" should probably be not-verifiable (because I can't see if transformers are shown)\n- Items with conditional applicability (\"Only when...\") should be n/a (because I can't verify the condition)\n\n\n- The grouping itself is triggered by whether transformer pads exist in the project. Without site plans, I can't confirm they're proposed, so the entire grouping should be marked n/a. The \"Emit All Statuses (override)\" instruction means I still need to include every item in the output, but they'd all be n/a with a note that no project documentation was available to assess transformer pad requirements.\n\nHowever, there's a distinction here—not having documents to verify something is different from the requirement not being applicable. If I can't determine applicability from available materials, that's a not-verifiable status, not n/a. So all items should be marked not-verifiable since I lack the necessary documents to evaluate them.\n\nI should also double-check the project directory path. The specified location appears empty, so I need to search more broadly for any plan files that might contain the information needed.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":387,"cache_read_input_tokens":33438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":387},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42ebeb32-1a8a-42fe-b8cc-11d9a764a570","uuid":"a526090c-ca73-43b4-9a4f-81b582b8374f"}
