{"level":30,"time":1778514181635,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YLChjeFe2oZSG6Cv4sYJYs","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Review Workflow - N independent review passes with cross-run consolidation\n     2→name: review\n     3→description: Ensemble review — runs N independent Haiku passes and consolidates findings with confidence tiers\n     4→version: 5.2.0\n     5→\n     6→requiredEnv:\n     7→  - OPENAI_API_KEY\n     8→\n     9→# Resources to prepare in workspace/ before starting workflow\n    10→resources:\n    11→  bureau: true\n    12→  submissionVersion: \"{{ input.submissionVersionId }}\"\n    13→  python: true\n    14→\n    15→# Input parameters\n    16→inputs:\n    17→  submissionVersionId:\n    18→    type: string\n    19→    required: true\n    20→    description: Submission version ID from Supabase\n    21→  jurisdiction:\n    22→    type: string\n    23→    required: true\n    24→    description: Jurisdiction slug (e.g., 'austin')\n    25→  guideCode:\n    26→    type: string\n    27→    required: true\n    28→    description: Discipline code (e.g., 'de', 'tr', 'fire')\n    29→  runs:\n    30→    type: number\n    31→    required: false\n    32→    default: 3\n    33→    description: Number of independent review runs\n    34→  model:\n    35→    type: string\n    36→    required: false\n    37→    default: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\n    38→    description: Model to use for review runs (cheap model — ensemble trades cost per run for N repetitions)\n    39→  effort:\n    40→    type: string\n    41→    required: false\n    42→    description: Agent effort level (low, medium, high). Only applied for models that support it (4.6+).\n    43→  eval:\n    44→    type: boolean\n    45→    required: false\n    46→    default: false\n    47→    description: Run evaluation against atomic MCR after review completes\n    48→  structureComments:\n    49→    type: boolean\n    50→    required: false\n    51→    default: true\n    52→    description: Run comment-structuring agent to organize findings into formatted review comments\n    53→  priorReviewId:\n    54→    type: string\n    55→    required: false\n    56→    default: \"\"\n    57→    description: Prior review ID for re-review comparison. When set, produces amended comments showing resolved vs outstanding issues.\n    58→  logAgentTrace:\n    59→    type: boolean\n    60→    required: false\n    61→    default: false\n    62→    description: When true, use the extended review schema (adds per-finding agentTrace) and populate review_comments.source_findings with raw per-run findings.\n    63→  logAllAgentTrace:\n    64→    type: boolean\n    65→    required: false\n    66→    default: false\n    67→    description: Strict superset of logAgentTrace — also emits findings for pass and n/a statuses (not just fail / not-verifiable).\n    68→  reviewSchemaName:\n    69→    type: string\n    70→    required: false\n    71→    default: review\n    72→    description: Review findings schema variant. Conductor overrides to 'reviewExtended' when logAgentTrace is set.\n    73→  reviewPromptName:\n    74→    type: string\n    75→    required: false\n    76→    default: review\n    77→    description: Review prompt variant (resolves to `prompts/<reviewPromptName>.md`). Conductor overrides to 'review-extended' when logAllAgentTrace is set. The extended prompt instructs the agent to emit findings for ALL statuses (pass / fail / not-verifiable / n/a) with always-on agentTrace; the production prompt skips pass / n/a findings.\n    78→  enabledVisionSpecialists:\n    79→    type: string\n    80→    required: false\n    81→    default: \"generic-vision,inspect-drawing,measure-distance\"\n    82→    description: |\n    83→      Comma-separated allow-list of vision specialists the `vision_check` dispatcher will route to.\n    84→      Accepted values: generic-vision, inspect-drawing, measure-distance. Whitespace around commas\n    85→      is trimmed. When the classifier picks a specialist not in this list, dispatch falls back\n    86→      to generic vision with `fallbackReason: specialist_disabled`. Lets us run ablation\n    87→      experiments (e.g. vision_check on review with inspect-drawing disabled to isolate the\n    88→      measure-distance signal). Only applies when `experiment=vision-check`.\n    89→\n    90→      Why CSV string vs array: workflow input schema only supports string|number|boolean\n    91→      uniformly. Conductor's vision_check dispatcher already comma-splits this value.\n    92→  setCurrent:\n    93→    type: boolean\n    94→    required: false\n    95→    default: true\n    96→    description: When true (default), the saved review is marked is_current=true and prior current reviews for the same project+department+version are retired. Pass --set-current=false to save the review as a non-current alternate (e.g. a parallel evaluation run); the existing current review is left untouched.\n    97→\n    98→# Where to upload when done\n    99→upload:\n   100→  bucket: workflow-runs\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02f3e714-877a-4005-af51-2af8f544a8d6","uuid":"b8073e18-0507-4ebd-ac5d-227c92e78a71","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/workflow/workflow.yaml","content":"# Review Workflow - N independent review passes with cross-run consolidation\nname: review\ndescription: Ensemble review — runs N independent Haiku passes and consolidates findings with confidence tiers\nversion: 5.2.0\n\nrequiredEnv:\n  - OPENAI_API_KEY\n\n# Resources to prepare in workspace/ before starting workflow\nresources:\n  bureau: true\n  submissionVersion: \"{{ input.submissionVersionId }}\"\n  python: true\n\n# Input parameters\ninputs:\n  submissionVersionId:\n    type: string\n    required: true\n    description: Submission version ID from Supabase\n  jurisdiction:\n    type: string\n    required: true\n    description: Jurisdiction slug (e.g., 'austin')\n  guideCode:\n    type: string\n    required: true\n    description: Discipline code (e.g., 'de', 'tr', 'fire')\n  runs:\n    type: number\n    required: false\n    default: 3\n    description: Number of independent review runs\n  model:\n    type: string\n    required: false\n    default: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\n    description: Model to use for review runs (cheap model — ensemble trades cost per run for N repetitions)\n  effort:\n    type: string\n    required: false\n    description: Agent effort level (low, medium, high). Only applied for models that support it (4.6+).\n  eval:\n    type: boolean\n    required: false\n    default: false\n    description: Run evaluation against atomic MCR after review completes\n  structureComments:\n    type: boolean\n    required: false\n    default: true\n    description: Run comment-structuring agent to organize findings into formatted review comments\n  priorReviewId:\n    type: string\n    required: false\n    default: \"\"\n    description: Prior review ID for re-review comparison. When set, produces amended comments showing resolved vs outstanding issues.\n  logAgentTrace:\n    type: boolean\n    required: false\n    default: false\n    description: When true, use the extended review schema (adds per-finding agentTrace) and populate review_comments.source_findings with raw per-run findings.\n  logAllAgentTrace:\n    type: boolean\n    required: false\n    default: false\n    description: Strict superset of logAgentTrace — also emits findings for pass and n/a statuses (not just fail / not-verifiable).\n  reviewSchemaName:\n    type: string\n    required: false\n    default: review\n    description: Review findings schema variant. Conductor overrides to 'reviewExtended' when logAgentTrace is set.\n  reviewPromptName:\n    type: string\n    required: false\n    default: review\n    description: Review prompt variant (resolves to `prompts/<reviewPromptName>.md`). Conductor overrides to 'review-extended' when logAllAgentTrace is set. The extended prompt instructs the agent to emit findings for ALL statuses (pass / fail / not-verifiable / n/a) with always-on agentTrace; the production prompt skips pass / n/a findings.\n  enabledVisionSpecialists:\n    type: string\n    required: false\n    default: \"generic-vision,inspect-drawing,measure-distance\"\n    description: |\n      Comma-separated allow-list of vision specialists the `vision_check` dispatcher will route to.\n      Accepted values: generic-vision, inspect-drawing, measure-distance. Whitespace around commas\n      is trimmed. When the classifier picks a specialist not in this list, dispatch falls back\n      to generic vision with `fallbackReason: specialist_disabled`. Lets us run ablation\n      experiments (e.g. vision_check on review with inspect-drawing disabled to isolate the\n      measure-distance signal). Only applies when `experiment=vision-check`.\n\n      Why CSV string vs array: workflow input schema only supports string|number|boolean\n      uniformly. Conductor's vision_check dispatcher already comma-splits this value.\n  setCurrent:\n    type: boolean\n    required: false\n    default: true\n    description: When true (default), the saved review is marked is_current=true and prior current reviews for the same project+department+version are retired. Pass --set-current=false to save the review as a non-current alternate (e.g. a parallel evaluation run); the existing current review is left untouched.\n\n# Where to upload when done\nuplo