{"level":30,"time":1778514193672,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NUMVu6kVa43meq4PWE11Pg","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Conductor\n     2→\n     3→YAML-based workflow orchestration engine that runs inside Vercel Sandboxes.\n     4→\n     5→## Architecture\n     6→\n     7→Architecture docs live in the controlroom workspace at `.claude/skills/architecture/`.\n     8→\n     9→## Coding Patterns\n    10→\n    11→- TypeScript with strict configuration\n    12→- Orchestrator handles state transitions, step executor handles agent/script runs\n    13→- Template engine (`{{ variable }}`) for dynamic values in workflow YAML\n    14→- Lock-free parallel execution - only main event loop touches shared state\n    15→- Structured logging events (anything you'd query/alert on in Better Stack) follow the convention in [`docs/structured-events.md`](./docs/structured-events.md): `event` (snake-case-dotted) + `category` fields, flat top-level shape\n    16→\n    17→## Danger Zones\n    18→\n    19→- NEVER modify workflow state from multiple threads - state transitions are single-threaded\n    20→- NEVER skip resource preparation - workflows expect bureau/site-plan files to exist\n    21→- NEVER hardcode paths - always use WORKSPACE_PATH and template variables\n    22→\n    23→## Dependencies\n    24→\n    25→- `ajv` and `ajv-cli` are production dependencies because bureau workflow agents use the `ajv` CLI binary at runtime inside sandboxes (e.g., review comment-structuring validates JSON output against schemas). Do not move these to devDependencies.\n    26→\n    27→## Dev Commands\n    28→\n    29→See README.md for CLI usage and development setup.\n    30→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe326180-34cb-4909-9447-54beae19d961","uuid":"0d781fe9-54a6-4661-981b-13a9e6e544ca","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/CLAUDE.md","content":"# Conductor\n\nYAML-based workflow orchestration engine that runs inside Vercel Sandboxes.\n\n## Architecture\n\nArchitecture docs live in the controlroom workspace at `.claude/skills/architecture/`.\n\n## Coding Patterns\n\n- TypeScript with strict configuration\n- Orchestrator handles state transitions, step executor handles agent/script runs\n- Template engine (`{{ variable }}`) for dynamic values in workflow YAML\n- Lock-free parallel execution - only main event loop touches shared state\n- Structured logging events (anything you'd query/alert on in Better Stack) follow the convention in [`docs/structured-events.md`](./docs/structured-events.md): `event` (snake-case-dotted) + `category` fields, flat top-level shape\n\n## Danger Zones\n\n- NEVER modify workflow state from multiple threads - state transitions are single-threaded\n- NEVER skip resource preparation - workflows expect bureau/site-plan files to exist\n- NEVER hardcode paths - always use WORKSPACE_PATH and template variables\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `ajv` and `ajv-cli` are production dependencies because bureau workflow agents use the `ajv` CLI binary at runtime inside sandboxes (e.g., review comment-structuring validates JSON output against schemas). Do not move these to devDependencies.\n\n## Dev Commands\n\nSee README.md for CLI usage and development setup.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778514193699,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCNRguWZRrzj1rrVi1cd24","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Site Plan: Valley View Townhomes\n     2→\n     3→**Site Address:** N/A\n     4→**Site Plan Number:** N/A\n     5→**Zoning:** N/A\n     6→\n     7→## Primary Site Plan (39 sheets)\n     8→\n     9→**Document ID (for vision tool):** `1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777`\n    10→\n    11→### Sheet Index\n    12→\n    13→- **Sheet 1 [Cover]:** Cover sheet containing project details, location map, and sheet index. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-01/guide.md`\n    14→- **Sheet 2 [Plat]:** Subdivision plat map showing legal boundaries, easements, and signatures. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-02/guide.md`\n    15→- **Sheet 3 [General Notes]:** Comprehensive general notes, sequence of construction, and project legend. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md`\n    16→- **Sheet 4 [Existing Conditions Survey]:** Topographic survey detailing existing structures, trees, and property boundaries. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-04/guide.md`\n    17→- **Sheet 5 [Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan]:** Site layout detailing erosion and sedimentation control measures. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-05/guide.md`\n    18→- **Sheet 6 [Erosion Control Notes]:** Contains erosion control, tree protection, and special construction notes. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-06/guide.md`\n    19→- **Sheet 7 [Erosion Control Details]:** Standard details and specifications for erosion and sediment control. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-07/guide.md`\n    20→- **Sheet 8 [Tree Removal & Demolition Plan]:** Site plan detailing existing structure demolition and tree removal. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-08/guide.md`\n    21→- **Sheet 9 [Site Plan]:** Detailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-09/guide.md`\n    22→- **Sheet 10 [Fire Protection Plan]:** Site plan illustrating fire lanes, hydrants, and fire zone details. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-10/guide.md`\n    23→- **Sheet 11 [Grading Plan]:** This sheet displays the detailed grading plan for the development site. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md`\n    24→- **Sheet 12 [Storm Sewer Plan]:** Displays the proposed storm sewer layout and drainage infrastructure details. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md`\n    25→- **Sheet 13 [Drainage Area Map]:** Existing and proposed drainage area maps with summary tables. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-13/guide.md`\n    26→- **Sheet 14 [Inlet Drainage Area Map]:** Site drainage area map and rational method runoff calculations. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-14/guide.md`\n    27→- **Sheet 15 [Biofiltration-Detention Pond Plan & Calculations]:** Biofiltration and detention pond plan, details, and engineering calculations. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-15/guide.md`\n    28→- **Sheet 16 [Biofiltration-Detention Pond Profiles]:** Biofiltration pond profiles, outfall details, and comprehensive maintenance requirements. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-16/guide.md`\n    29→- **Sheet 17 [Conveyance Cross Sections]:** Conveyance cross-section graphs and corresponding site plan view. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-17/guide.md`\n    30→- **Sheet 18 [Austin Water General Information & Construction Notes]:** Austin Water general information, construction notes, and flow tests. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-18/guide.md`\n    31→- **Sheet 19 [Utility Tap Plan]:** Utility tap plan showing proposed water and wastewater connections. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-19/guide.md`\n    32→- **Sheet 20 [Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile]:** Utility tap public plan and profile for townhomes project. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-20/guide.md`\n    33→- **Sheet 21 [Preliminary Electrical Design Plan]:** Layout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md`\n    34→- **Sheet 22 [Construction Details 1]:** Construction details for curbs, sidewalks, driveways, and bicycle parking. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-22/guide.md`\n    35→- **Sheet 23 [Construction Details 2]:** Standard construction details for water infrastructure, valves, and fire hydrants. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-23/guide.md`\n    36→- **Sheet 24 [Construction Details 3]:** Standard construction details for water services and trench repairs. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-24/guide.md`\n    37→- **Sheet 25 [Construction Details 4]:** Standard details, plan, and section views for fire line meters. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-25/guide.md`\n    38→- **Sheet 26 [Construction Details 5]:** Standard details for wastewater service connections and sewer cleanouts. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-26/guide.md`\n    39→- **Sheet 27 [Construction Details 6]:** Construction details for wastewater manholes and duplex grinder pumps. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-27/guide.md`\n    40→- **Sheet 28 [Construction Details 7]:** Construction details for storm drain manholes and catch basins. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-28/guide.md`\n    41→- **Sheet 29 [Addressing Plan]:** Site plan showing building layouts and individual unit addresses. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md`\n    42→- **Sheet 30 [Existing Tree Plan]:** Site plan displaying existing trees, protection measures, and care notes. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-30/guide.md`\n    43→- **Sheet 31 [Landscape Plan]:** Landscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md`\n    44→- **Sheet 32 [Tree List]:** This page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md`\n    45→- **Sheet 33 [Canopy Impact Exhibit]:** Exhibits detailing tree canopy calculations and construction impact analysis. → `primary-site-plan/sheet-33/guide.md`\n    46→- **Sheet 34 [Root Zone Impact Exhibit]:** Critical root zone impact diagrams, calculations, and tree photos. → 