{"level":30,"time":1778514947551,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NSfHpDys4vFCXSpoqx1duA","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — North arrow and graphical scale for the drawing.\n     4→\n     5→NORTH\n     6→[North Arrow Symbol]\n     7→SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\n     8→0 10 20 50\n     9→\n    10→## Block 2: drawing — A detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of buildings, parking lots, landscaping areas, and other site features. The drawing includes contours, property lines, utility lines, and symbols corresponding to the key notes.\n    11→\n    12→This block contains a complex site plan drawing. It illustrates the layout of the proposed townhomes, parking areas, and surrounding landscaping. Key features include:\n    13→- Building footprints\n    14→- Parking lot with designated spaces and landscaping islands\n    15→- Sidewalks and pathways\n    16→- Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\n    17→- Contour lines with elevation labels (e.g., 680, 681, 682)\n    18→- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\n    19→- Fences marked with 'X' along the property lines\n    20→- Various key note symbols (e.g., H.1, H.2, H.3) referencing the legend\n    21→- Text labels indicating specific areas or features (e.g., 'Valley View Road', 'Existing Stone Retaining Wall')\n    22→- Coordinates and station numbers along the edges\n    23→\n    24→## Block 4: notes — General notes regarding landscape requirements, including finished elevations for parking lot islands and supplemental irrigation during drought stages.\n    25→\n    26→NOTE:\n    27→FINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\n    28→IF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\n    29→SUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\n    30→FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n    31→\n    32→## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n    33→\n    34→KEY NOTES:\n    35→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n    36→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n    37→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n    38→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n    39→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n    40→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n    41→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\n    42→SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    43→PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    44→P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n    45→M - MITIGATION TREE\n    46→\n    47→## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n    48→\n    49→OWNER:\n    50→WM 41 AUSTIN\n    51→RE, LLC\n    52→\n    53→## Block 8: text_block — Address of the project location.\n    54→\n    55→PROJECT LOCATION:\n    56→3759 VALLEY\n    57→VIEW ROAD,\n    58→AUSTIN,\n    59→TEXAS 78704\n    60→\n    61→## Block 9: text_block — Name of the project.\n    62→\n    63→PROJECT NAME:\n    64→VALLEY VIEW\n    65→TOWNHOMES\n    66→\n    67→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02f3e714-877a-4005-af51-2af8f544a8d6","uuid":"5609faad-b2c4-47b1-b799-427c22acfdf4","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/wip/measure-distance-tool/vv-el-run/2026-04-15/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — North arrow and graphical scale for the drawing.\n\nNORTH\n[North Arrow Symbol]\nSCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\n0 10 20 50\n\n## Block 2: drawing — A detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of buildings, parking lots, landscaping areas, and other site features. The drawing includes contours, property lines, utility lines, and symbols corresponding to the key notes.\n\nThis block contains a complex site plan drawing. It illustrates the layout of the proposed townhomes, parking areas, and surrounding landscaping. Key features include:\n- Building footprints\n- Parking lot with designated spaces and landscaping islands\n- Sidewalks and pathways\n- Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\n- Contour lines with elevation labels (e.g., 680, 681, 682)\n- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\n- Fences marked with 'X' along the property lines\n- Various key note symbols (e.g., H.1, H.2, H.3) referencing the legend\n- Text labels indicating specific areas or features (e.g., 'Valley View Road', 'Existing Stone Retaining Wall')\n- Coordinates and station numbers along the edges\n\n## Block 4: notes — General notes regarding landscape requirements, including finished elevations for parking lot islands and supplemental irrigation during drought stages.\n\nNOTE:\nFINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\nIF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\nSUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\nFOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n\n## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n\nKEY NOTES:\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\nSY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nPL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nP - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\nM - MITIGATION TREE\n\n## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n\nOWNER:\nWM 41 AUSTIN\nRE, LLC\n\n## Block 8: text_block — Address of the project location.\n\nPROJECT LOCATION:\n3759 VALLEY\nVIEW ROAD,\nAUSTIN,\nTEXAS 78704\n\n## Block 9: text_block — Name of the project.\n\nPROJECT NAME:\nVALLEY VIEW\nTOWNHOMES\n\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778514947551,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P2epFbr6Jbyvy6SQhxRy2X","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 35 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: notes — Notes related to tree preservation calculations.\n     4→\n     5→NOTES:\n     6→1. CHINABERRY AND BRADFORD PEAR ARE INVASIVE TREES AND REQUIRE NO MITIGATION.\n     7→2. ASH TREES REQUIRE NO MITIGATION DUE TO EMERALD ASH BORER.\n     8→\n     9→## Block 3: notes — Notes on special construction techniques.\n    10→\n    11→SPECIAL CONSTRUCTION TECHNIQUES\n    12→ECM 3.5.4 (D)\n    13→1. PRIOR TO EXCAVATION WITHIN TREE DRIP LINES OR THE REMOVAL OF\n    14→TREES ADJACENT TO OTHER TREES THAT ARE TO REMAIN, MAKE A\n    15→CLEAN CUT BETWEEN THE DISTURBED AND UNDISTURBED ROOT ZONES\n    16→WITH A ROCK SAW OR SIMILAR EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n    17→2. IN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS THAT CANNOT BE PROTECTED DURING\n    18→CONSTRUCTION WITH FENCING AND WHERE HEAVY VEHICULAR TRAFFIC\n    19→IS ANTICIPATED, COVER THOSE AREAS WITH A MINIMUM OF 12 INCHES OF\n    20→ORGANIC MULCH TO MINIMIZE SOIL COMPACTION. IN AREAS WITH HIGH\n    21→SOIL PLASTICITY GEOTEXTILE FABRIC, PER STANDARD SPECIFICATION\n    22→620S, SHOULD BE PLACED UNDER THE MULCH TO PREVENT EXCESSIVE\n    23→MIXING OF THE SOIL AND MULCH. ADDITIONALLY, MATERIAL SUCH AS\n    24→PLYWOOD AND METAL SHEETS, COULD BE REQUIRED BY THE CITY\n    25→ARBORIST TO MINIMIZE ROOT IMPACTS FROM HEAVY EQUIPMENT.\n    26→3. ONCE THE PROJECT IS COMPLETED, ALL MATERIALS SHOULD BE\n    27→REMOVED, AND THE MULCH SHOULD BE REDUCED TO A DEPTH OF 3\n    28→INCHES. PERFORM ALL GRADING WITHIN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS BY\n    29→HAND OR WITH SMALL EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n    30→4. WATER ALL TREES MOST HEAVILY IMPACTED BY CONSTRUCTION\n    31→ACTIVITIES DEEPLY ONCE A WEEK DURING ACCUMULATION OF THE\n    32→LEAVES.\n    33→5. WHEN INSTALLING CONCRETE ADJACENT TO THE ROOT ZONE OF A TREE,\n    34→USE A PLASTIC VAPOR BARRIER BEHIND THE CONCRETE TO PROHIBIT\n    35→LEACHING OF LIME INTO THE SOIL.\n    36→\n    37→## Block 5: notes — Plant list section heading.\n    38→\n    39→PLANT LIST\n    40→\n    41→## Block 6: notes — Notes related to the plant list.\n    42→\n    43→NOTES:\n    44→1. THE CONTRACTORS (GENERAL AND SUBCONTRACTORS) SHALL PROVIDE UNIT COSTS FOR ALL\n    45→SOFTSCAPE AND HARDSCAPE MATERIAL SPECIFIED ON THE DRAWINGS AND SPECIFICATIONS. UNIT\n    46→COSTS SHALL BE PROVIDED FOR MATERIALS AND INSTALLATION SEPARATELY. UNIT COSTS SHALL\n    47→BE: 'EACH' FOR PLANT MATERIAL, 'SQUARE FOOT' OR 'SQUARE YARD' FOR PAVEMENTS, LINEAR FOOT\n    48→FOR WALL AND FENCE, 'EACH' FOR SITE FURNISHINGS AND SITE AMENITIES, 'CUBIC YARD' OR 'CUBIC\n    49→FOOT' FOR SOIL, MULCH AND OTHER BULK PRODUCTS AND 'EACH' OR 'LUMP SUM' FOR\n    50→MISCELLANEOUS ITEMS. THE UNIT COST SHALL BE FORMATTED TO HAVE COLUMNS FOR; ITEMS, UNIT,\n    51→UNIT COST, TOTAL ITEM COST.\n    52→2. PLANT QUANTITIES ARE PROVIDED FOR OWNER CONVENIENCE ONLY. CONTRACTOR IS\n    53→RESPONSIBLE FOR VERIFYING AND PROVIDING PLANT QUANTITIES SHOWN ON THE LANDSCAPE PLAN.\n    54→3. CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR LOCATING AND SECURING TREE AND PLANT MATERIAL IN\n    55→ADVANCE. BECAUSE OF THE LONG LEAD TIME ON THIS INSTALLATION AND THE RECENT SHORTAGE\n    56→ON TREE CROP, CONTRACTOR SHALL RESERVE OR CONTRACT GROW TREES WITH A GROWER.\n    57→\n    58→## Block 11: table — Header for City of Austin Tree Preservation Calculations.\n    59→\n    60→CITY OF AUSTIN\n    61→TREE PRESERVATION CALCULATIONS:\n    62→\n    63→## Block 12: table — Calculations related to tree preservation.\n    64→\n    65→EXISTING TREES:\n    66→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 212 INCHES\n    67→(HERITAGE)\n    68→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 0 INCHES\n    69→(NON HERITAGE)\n    70→19 TO 23.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES 99 INCHES\n    71→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES 295 INCHES\n    72→19 INCHES AND GREATER, ALL OTHER TREES 0 INCHES\n    73→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ALL OTHER TREES 66 INCHES\n    74→\n    75→TREES REMOVED\n    76→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 27 INCHES\n    77→(HERITAGE):\n    78→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 0 INCHES\n    79→(NON HERITAGE):\n    80→19 TO 23.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 79 INCHES\n    81→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 134 INCHES\n    82→19 INCHES AND GREATER, ALL OTHER TREES: 0 INCHES\n    83→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ALL OTHER TREES: 66 INCHES\n    84→TOTAL: 288 INCHES\n    85→\n    86→REPLACEMENT INCHES REQUIRED\n    87→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 40.5 INCHES\n    88→(HERITAGE): 300%\n    89→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 0 INCHES\n    90→(NON HERITAGE): 100%\n    91→19 TO 23.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 100% 79 INCHES\n    92→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 50% 82 INCHES\n    93→19 INCHES AND GREATER, ALL OTHER TREES: 50% 0 INCHES\n    94→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ALL OTHER TREES: 25% 15.5 INCHES\n    95→TOTAL: 217 INCHES\n    96→\n    97→URBAN FORESTRY INFORMATION\n    98→TOTAL APP F TREE INCHES SURVEYED 606 INCHES\n    99→TOTAL APP F TREE INCHES REMOVED 240 INCHES\n   100→TOTAL INVASIVE TREE INCHES REMOVED 137 INCHES\n   101→\n   102→TOTAL MITIGATION INCHES PLANTED ON SITE 55 INCHES\n   103→REMAINING MITIGATION INCHES REQUIRED 162 INCHES\n   104→\n   105→MITIGATION DEFICIT (REPLACE REMAINING AT $32,400\n   106→STANDARD $200 PER INCH)\n   107→HB7 MITIGATION CREDIT (55x50%x$200) $5,500\n   108→AMOUNT TO BE PAID INTO FUND $26,900\n   109→\n   110→## Block 13: table — Table listing shade trees.\n   111→\n   112→SHADE TREES\n   113→\n   114→| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. SPEC. |\n   115→|---|---|---|---|\n   116→| [circle with dot] | | EXISTING TREE, TO BE PERSERVED | |\n   117→| [circle with cross] | 2 | LIVE OAK, QUERCUS VIRGINIANA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN |\n