{"level":30,"time":1778515018752,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012b3r3BA5x2kgvcmAXjwazf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is critical! The vision check found proposed trees ('B M' in southwest corner and 'M' cluster in southeast) that are extremely close to overhead electric lines:\n- 'B M' tree: 0.4 feet from OHE line (well within the 15-foot minimum)\n- 'M' cluster: 1.1 feet from OHE line (well within the 15-foot minimum)\n\nThis suggests a significant potential violation. I need to:\n1. Determine which tree species these are (B M and M markers)\n2. Check if they are utility-compatible\n3. Check the mature heights to see if they are \"large trees\"\n\nFrom the plant list I read earlier:\n- M = MITIGATION TREE (but what species?)\n- P = PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n- PL = PARKING LOT TREE\n- SY = STREET YARD TREE\n\nI need to find the detailed plant list that shows which species are marked as \"M\" and \"B M\". Let me look for more details about the plant list on the landscape plan.\n\nBut wait - the measurement says the OHE line is at the southern boundary. This could be an existing utility line that runs along the boundary of the property. The trees being so close (0.4 feet) seems odd - that would mean the trees are almost touching the OHE line at the property boundary.\n\nLet me look at the orientation and context more carefully. The vision tool is saying it's measuring from proposed trees to OHE lines, so this is definitely a concern that needs to be flagged.\n\nI should make more vision_check calls to understand:\n1. What species are the proposed trees that are near OHE?\n2. Are these mitigation trees or required trees?\n3. Are clearance zones properly indicated on the landscape plan?","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_detail