{"level":30,"time":1778515046312,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cu5XKLnkuWSYoJPPiVwJdS","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document (identified as \"LANDSCAPE PLAN\", sheet 28 of 35), here is the information regarding overhead electric utility lines:\n\n**Presence and Location of Overhead Lines:**\nYes, overhead electric utility lines are shown on this site plan. They are indicated by lines containing the repeating text label **\"-OHE-\"**.\n\nRelative to the proposed buildings, these lines are located in two primary areas:\n1.  **Along the left property frontage:** An \"-OHE-\" line runs vertically along the far-left edge of the drawing, within or adjacent to the right-of-way labeled \"Valley View Road\". This line is separated from the left-most building facade by an area of proposed paving (shaded gray and labeled \"H.1\") and a street yard area.\n2.  **Along the bottom property edge:** An \"-OHE-\" line runs horizontally along the entire bottom edge (southern edge, based on the North arrow) of the site. It runs parallel to the long, bottom-facing wall of the proposed building complex, separated by a strip of land that includes proposed trees and another utility line labeled \"-SD-\".\n\nThere are no \"-OHE-\" lines shown crossing through the center of the site or running between the individual building units.\n\n**Clearance Dimensions:**\nScanning the areas between the building footprints and the \"-OHE-\" lines, **there are no clearance dimensions shown on this specific sheet.** There are no dimension lines indicating the distance from the building facades to the overhead utility lines."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02f3e714-877a-4005-af51-2af8f544a8d6","uuid":"e42035b2-2ba9-476b-8030-b9fdd9e197a2","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document (identified as \"LANDSCAPE PLAN\", sheet 28 of 35), here is the information regarding overhead electric utility lines:\n\n**Presence and Location of Overhead Lines:**\nYes, overhead electric utility lines are shown on this site plan. They are indicated by lines containing the repeating text label **\"-OHE-\"**.\n\nRelative to the proposed buildings, these lines are located in two primary areas:\n1.  **Along the left property frontage:** An \"-OHE-\" line runs vertically along the far-left edge of the drawing, within or adjacent to the right-of-way labeled \"Valley View Road\". This line is separated from the left-most building facade by an area of proposed paving (shaded gray and labeled \"H.1\") and a street yard area.\n2.  **Along the bottom property edge:** An \"-OHE-\" line runs horizontally along the entire bottom edge (southern edge, based on the North arrow) of the site. It runs parallel to the long, bottom-facing wall of the proposed building complex, separated by a strip of land that includes proposed trees and another utility line labeled \"-SD-\".\n\nThere are no \"-OHE-\" lines shown crossing through the center of the site or running between the individual building units.\n\n**Clearance Dimensions:**\nScanning the areas between the building footprints and the \"-OHE-\" lines, **there are no clearance dimensions shown on this specific sheet.** There are no dimension lines indicating the distance from the building facades to the overhead utility lines."}]}
