shown together on this landscape plan. \n*   **Proposed Trees:** The plan displays numerous tree symbols which are identified in the Key Notes legend as:\n    *   \"SY - STREET YARD TREE...\"\n    *   \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE...\"\n    *   \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n    *   \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"\n*   **Overhead Electric (OHE):** A utility line labeled specifically as \"--- OHE ---\" runs along the bottom edge of the site plan area.\n*   **Spatial Relationship:** Several proposed tree symbols (including those labeled with \"M\" for Mitigation Tree) are placed directly adjacent to or underneath this \"--- OHE ---\" line along that bottom boundary, allowing their spatial relationship to be seen.\n\n**2. Are clearance dimensions or clearance zone notes annotated on the landscape plan where trees are near OHE?**\nNo. After carefully reviewing the plan specifically where the trees intersect or sit near the \"--- OHE ---\" line, as well as checking all general notes (\"IRRIGATION NOTES\", \"NOTE:\", and \"KEY NOTES:\"), there are **no** clearance dimensions, clearance zone boundaries, or specific annotations regarding required clearances between the proposed trees and the overhead electric lines."}]}
