{"level":30,"time":1778516204653,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VgNEipEk6BZxMZGqJxkWnh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the \"M\" trees are confirmed to be MITIGATION trees, but their specific species cannot be identified from the landscape plan itself. The species are presumably identified on Sheet 35 (the Plant List sheet), but those are the overall selected mitigation species.\n\nHowever, the fact that mitigation trees are being placed 0.4-1.1 feet from an OHE line without any documentation or notes indicating approval for this placement is itself a major violation.\n\nNow let me systematically evaluate each checklist item. Based on my research:\n\n**Key Findings:**\n1. **Overhead Electric Facilities Present:** YES - OHE lines are shown on the landscape plan running along the southern boundary\n2. **Proposed Trees Near OHE:** YES - Multiple trees (M symbols and B M symbol) are 0.4-1.1 feet from OHE line\n3. **Tree Species Identification on Plan:** NO - Species are not identified on Sheet 31 landscape plan (deficiency EL-2.10)\n4. **Clearance Dimensions/Annotations:** NO - No clearances dimensioned or annotated on landscape plan (potential deficiency EL-2.12, EL-2.13, EL-2.14)\n5. **Clearance Verification:** Trees at 0.4-1.1 feet are far below any permitted clearance (15 feet for distribution, 50 feet for transmission)\n6. **No Austin Energy Approval:** Not mentioned in the documentation reviewed (deficiency EL-2.15)\n\n**Checklist Item Evaluation:**\n\n**EL-2.1**: Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 feet of distribution - Trees at 0.4-1.1 feet without species identification = likely FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-2.2**: Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 feet of transmission - Insufficient data on transmission lines = N/A or NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n\n**EL-2.3**: Cedar Elm and Live Oak from the mitigation plant list are both large trees (40+ feet) positioned 0.4-1.1 feet from distribution lines, well within the 25-foot threshold = FAIL\n\n**EL-2.4**: Large trees near transmission - Transmission line status unclear = N/A or NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-2.5**: Trees in transmission easement - Facts.md identifies 5' and 7.5' electric easements rather than transmission easement = N/A\n\n**EL-2.6**: Trees within 10 feet of poles - Pole locations need verification on site\n\n**EL-2.7**: Trees within 10 feet of pad\n\n-mounted equipment - Equipment locations require field verification\n\n**EL-2.8**: Underground electric equipment shown on Facts.md and Sheet 21, but trees within 5 feet need distance confirmation\n\n**EL-2.9**: Root barriers for trees within 20 feet of underground equipment - Distances and barrier presence cannot be confirmed from plans\n\n**EL-2.10**: Plant legend on Sheet 31 fails to identify species = FAIL\n\n**EL-2.11**: Large trees lack differentiation on the landscape plan = FAIL\n\n**EL-2.12**: Clearances not dimensioned from pole locations = NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-2.13**: Clearances not dimensioned from trunk versus canopy = NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-2.14**: Trees not shown in relation to electrical infrastructure on plans\n\n, though both elements are present = FAIL/NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-2.15**: No Austin Energy approval documentation for trees in prohibited zones = FAIL\n\nNeed to conduct field observations to validate the clearance requirements in EL-2.6 through EL-2.9.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1299,"cache_read_input_tokens":64719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1299},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c8f4369-ba37-4038-94f5-e0bc36accce4","uuid":"