ne.\n\n**Are the tree types identified, and can they be cross-referenced against the Utility Compatible list?**\nNo, the specific botanical or common tree types (species) are **not** identified on this specific page. Because only functional classification codes (SY, PL, P, M) are provided without a corresponding plant schedule detailing the exact species, it is **not possible** to cross-reference the trees shown against a Utility Compatible list using only this document. A supplementary plant list or schedule from the broader submission would be required to verify species compatibility with the overhead lines."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02f3e714-877a-4005-af51-2af8f544a8d6","uuid":"5083ea87-edaa-4036-9aed-845d69269fa6","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the answers to your specific questions:\n\n**What trees are shown on the landscape plan?**\nThe landscape plan shows numerous trees represented by circular graphics of varying sizes, located primarily around the perimeter of the site and near parking areas. According to the \"KEY NOTES\" section on the right side of the drawing, the trees are categorized by the following letter codes, which appear inside or next to the tree symbols on the plan:\n*   **\"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"**\n*   **\"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"**\n*   **\"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"**\n*   **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**\n\nFor example, trees along the left side (Valley View Road) are labeled \"SY\" and \"SY/M\". Trees along the top and bottom edges include labels for \"M\" and \"PL\".\n\n**Are there any trees planted within 10 feet of the overhead electric utility lines marked as OHE?**\nYes. The overhead electric line, labeled as a dashed line with **\"-OHE-\"**, runs horizontally along the bottom edge of the property line shown on the plan. Utilizing the graphical scale provided in the bottom right corner (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), there appear to be trees planted or existing within 10 feet of this line. Specifically, near the bottom right corner of the site plan, there is a cluster of tree symbols. The center points (trunks) of at least two trees in this area—one of which is labeled **\"M\"** (Mitigation Tree)—appear visually to be within 10 feet of the OHE line, and their drawn canopies directly overlap the OHE line.\n\n**Are the tree types identified, and can they be cross-referenced against the Utility Compatible list?**\nNo, the specific botanical or common tree types (species) are **not** identified on this specific page. Because only functional classification codes (SY, PL, P, M) are provided without a corresponding plant schedule detailing the exact species, it is **not possible** to cross-reference the trees shown against a Utility Compatible list using only this document. A supplementary plant list or schedule from the broader submission would be required to verify species compatibility with the overhead lines."}]}
