{"level":30,"time":1778516470899,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01NgFXG74UeK9fZHm1iUQQT2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V5WWKJnErgRcgBor1L9LnD","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary where OHE distribution line intersects landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Sheet 35 - Landscape Calculations (Plant List)"}],"comment":"Proposed trees (specifically mitigation trees marked 'M') are positioned 0.4-1.1 feet from the overhead electric distribution line, far below the 15-foot minimum clearance requirement. Tree species on the landscape plan are not identified by name (only by functional symbol), preventing verification of utility compatibility status. The proposed plant list includes Live Oak and Cedar Elm, which are large trees (40+ feet mature height) requiring 25-foot clearance for distribution lines. Trees are positioned within prohibited zone without documented Austin Energy approval.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of landscape plan shows proposed trees labeled 'M' and 'B M' positioned 0.4-1.1 feet laterally from OHE line on southern boundary (Sheet 31). Tree species are not identified on the landscape plan itself, only functional categories (M, SY, PL, P). Proposed plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists Live Oak and Cedar Elm as mitigation/shade trees. No clearance annotations or Austin Energy approval letters found in site plan documentation.","reasoning":"The 0.4-1.1 foot distances are well below the 15-foot minimum clearance required by UCM § 1.10.10.4 for distribution facilities. Even if these trees were utility-compatible species, the distance violation is a deficiency. The inability to verify species compatibility from the landscape plan itself compounds the issue. The plant list includes species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm) that are not utility-compatible for distances less than 15 feet per ECM Appendix F, and these are large trees requiring 25-foot clearance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission electric lines (voltage ≥60kV) are identified on the site plan or in the project facts. Facts.md identifies only 5-foot and 7.5-foot electric easements (distribution infrastructure). The overhead line shown on the landscape plan is labeled as 'OHE' (overhead electric) distribution, not transmission. This requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md lists easements as 5-foot and 7.5-foot electric easements (distribution). Landscape plan (Sheet 31) labels overhead line as 'OHE' (distribution). No transmission lines, transmission easements, or transmission voltage levels (60kV+) mentioned in any site plan documentation.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when transmission lines are present. The site has distribution infrastructure only. Transmission facilities are physically larger with dedicated easements and higher voltage (69kV, 138kV, 345kV). Absence of transmission-related documentation and labels indicates this infrastructure is not present on the project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary where OHE distribution line intersects landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Sheet 35 - Landscape Calculations (Plant List with Species)"}],"comment":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) are proposed within 25 feet of overhead electric distribution conductors. The proposed plant schedule on Sheet 35 specifies Cedar Elm and Live Oak as shade trees to be planted. Both species are listed in ECM Appendix F with mature heights of 40+ feet, meeting the definition of 'large trees.' Vision measurement shows proposed mitigation trees positioned only 0.4-1.1 feet from the OHE line, far below the 25-foot minimum clearance required for large trees from distribution lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 plant list identifies 10 Cedar Elm (ULMUS CRASSIFOLIA) and 2 Live Oak (QUERCUS VIRGINIANA) as proposed shade trees with minimum 100-gallon, 4-inch caliper specifications. ECM Appendix F lists both species with mature heights of 40+ feet. Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows 'M' (mitigation) trees positioned 0.4-1.1 feet from OHE line. No clearance verification annotations present on landscape plan.","reasoning":"Cedar Elm and Live Oak are documented as large trees (40+ feet mature height). Per ECM Appendix F, these trees require 25-foot clearance from distribution conductors. The measured distance of 0.4-1.1 feet is a clearance violation. Large tree designation is not differentiated on the landscape plan, preventing visual verification of this requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission electric facilities are identified on the site. This requirement applies only when transmission lines are present. Requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md and site plan documentation show distribution infrastructure only (5-foot and 7.5-foot electric easements). No transmission easements, transmission lines, or transmission voltage facilities identified.","reasoning":"This requirement is gated by presence of transmission infrastructure. Transmission facilities are not shown or referenced on the site plan.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is identified on the site. Facts.md documents two recorded electric easements (5-foot and 7.5-foot) which are plat-dedicated distribution easements, not transmission easements. The categorical prohibition against trees in transmission easements does not apply to distribution easements. This requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md lists plat-dedicated 5-foot and 7.5-foot electric easements recorded in Mecey Subdivision plat. These are distribution voltage easements. No transmission easement document references found. Landscape plan does not show a transmission easement boundary.","reasoning":"The prohibition on trees within transmission easement boundaries applies only when a transmission easement exists. The recorded easements are distribution (lower voltage) facilities. The requirement does not apply to distribution easements.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electric utility pole locations are not depicted on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). While overhead electric lines are shown and labeled, specific pole positions and pole centerline locations are not marked. Therefore, the clearance distance from proposed trees to poles cannot be verified from the landscape plan. Poles must be shown to enable verification of the 10-foot lateral clearance requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows overhead electric line labeled 'OHE' but does not include pole location symbols or designations (no 'PP' or 'UP' symbols or pole markers visible). Vision check confirmed poles are not shown on this sheet.","reasoning":"Without pole locations marked on the landscape plan, tree-to-pole clearances cannot be measured or verified. The requirement cannot be evaluated from available plan documentation. This is not a pass because poles must be shown to enable verification per the requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No pad-mounted electric equipment (transformers or connection boxes) is depicted on the landscape plan. Utility Plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical service routing with transformers, pull boxes, and meters, but these are underground facilities, not pad-mounted equipment. No pad-mounted equipment is identified as present or proposed on site. This requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not show pad-mounted transformer symbols. Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground transformers and pull boxes. No pad-mount equipment locations identified on landscape plan or utility plan.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when pad-mounted electric equipment is present or proposed. The site has underground electrical infrastructure, not pad-mounted equipment. Requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site where underground electric equipment is proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electric equipment (transformers, pull boxes) is shown on Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan), but the spatial relationship between these underground facilities and proposed trees on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) cannot be determined from the available documentation. Exact locations of underground equipment and proposed trees must be cross-referenced with dimensioned clearances to verify compliance with the 5-foot lateral clearance requirement. No clearance dimensions or cross-references between the electrical plan and landscape plan are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electrical transformers and pull boxes located throughout the site. Sheet 31 shows proposed trees (SY, PL, P, M symbols) but does not reference underground equipment locations or show clearance distances to underground facilities. The two plans use the same coordinate system but clearance distances are not annotated on either plan.","reasoning":"While underground equipment is shown on the electrical plan and trees are shown on the landscape plan, there is no documentation of clearance distances between them. Without dimensioned distances or cross-sheet annotations indicating clearances, compliance with the 5-foot lateral clearance requirement cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site where underground electric equipment is within 20 feet of proposed trees"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Root barriers are required only for trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment. However, because clearance distances between proposed trees and underground equipment have not been documented or dimensioned on the plans (see EL-2.8), it cannot be determined which trees, if any, are within the 20-foot root barrier trigger distance. Additionally, no root barrier details, specifications, or notes are visible on Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) indicating where root barriers have been designed. This requirement cannot be verified from the available documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan does not show underground electric equipment locations, does not dimension clearances to equipment, and does not include root barrier specifications or details. Sheet 21 shows underground equipment but does not cross-reference tree locations. No standard details or notes on Sheet 37 (Landscape Details) or other sheets specify root barrier designs as required.","reasoning":"Root barrier requirements are conditional on distance (20 feet) to underground equipment. Without documented clearances (per EL-2.8), the trigger condition cannot be established. Furthermore, if root barriers were required, their specifications and locations are not documented on the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) - entire drawing where proposed trees are shown near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Sheet 35 - Landscape Calculations (contains plant species list)"}],"comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) identifies proposed trees only by functional category symbols (SY=Street Yard Tree, PL=Parking Lot Tree, P=Parking Buffer Point Tree, M=Mitigation Tree). Tree species (common and scientific names) are not provided on the landscape plan. While a detailed plant schedule with species identification exists on Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations), tree species cannot be identified directly from the landscape plan itself where clearance verification is needed. Trees shown near overhead electric facilities on Sheet 31 must have their species clearly identified on that sheet to enable verification of utility compatibility and other electric facility clearance requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) confirmed that tree symbols are labeled only with functional categories (SY, PL, P, M) and are defined in the key notes only by these functional designations, not by species names. Common and scientific tree names appear only on Sheet 35 (separate sheet), not on Sheet 31 where clearances must be verified.","reasoning":"The landscape plan is the primary document for verifying tree/utility clearances. Species identification directly on this plan is necessary to cross-check against ECM Appendix F (UC status, mature height) and verify compliance with clearance requirements. Requiring reviewers to flip to another sheet to identify tree species is not adequate documentation. This is a convention deficiency in plan presentation.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) - areas where large trees (40+ feet mature height) are proposed near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Sheet 35 - Landscape Calculations (Plant List showing Cedar Elm and Live Oak with container sizes)"}],"comment":"Large trees proposed near overhead electric facilities are not differentiated from smaller trees on the landscape plan. The plant schedule on Sheet 35 specifies Cedar Elm (10 plants at 100 gallons) and Live Oak (2 plants at 100 gallons) - both large trees with 40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F. These large trees require 25-foot clearance from distribution facilities, but on the landscape plan they are shown with the same symbol (SY for Street Yard Tree) as smaller trees, with no notation of their large size status. This makes it impossible to quickly identify which proposed trees trigger the more restrictive 25-foot (versus 15-foot) clearance requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows all street yard trees and shade trees with uniform 'SY' symbol, with no size differentiation or notation of mature height (40+ feet). Plant schedule on Sheet 35 identifies Cedar Elm and Live Oak as 100-gallon minimum, which denotes large trees, but this is not cross-referenced or marked on the landscape plan where clearances must be verified.","reasoning":"Large trees (40+ feet mature height) have different clearance requirements than small/medium trees. A reviewer cannot determine from the landscape plan alone whether a proposed 'SY' tree is a large tree requiring 25-foot clearance or a smaller tree allowing 15-foot clearance. Standard practice is to differentiate large trees with notation or symbol on the landscape plan.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) - areas where tree clearances should be dimensioned"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are provided on the landscape plan. Therefore, compliance with the measurement methodology (from tree trunk center to outside conductor, not from pole centerline) cannot be verified. If clearance dimensions were to be added to the plan, they must originate from the conductor location, not from the pole centerline. The grouping guide notes that overhead conductors are offset laterally from poles (typically 4+ feet), so measuring from pole center significantly underestimates clearance. Current plan documentation does not provide any dimension lines or callouts that would allow assessment of measurement reference points.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows proposed trees and OHE line but contains no dimension lines, clearance annotations, or distance callouts between trees and the electric line. No reference points or measurement methodology are indicated on the plan.","reasoning":"Without dimensions on the plan, the measurement methodology cannot be evaluated. This is not necessarily a fail (plans sometimes show distances in other ways), but it is not verifiable from the submitted documentation. The requirement that measurements originate from the outside conductor (not pole centerline) cannot be confirmed from unannoted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) - areas where tree clearances should be dimensioned"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are provided on the landscape plan. Therefore, compliance with the measurement methodology (from tree trunk center/planting location, not from canopy edge) cannot be verified. If clearance dimensions were to be added to the plan, dimension lines must terminate at the tree symbol/trunk location, not at a projected canopy edge. Since no clearance dimensions are shown, the reference point for tree measurements cannot be assessed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols (circles with various marks for SY, PL, P, M categories) but contains no dimension lines terminating at tree locations to indicate measurement reference points. No callouts specify trunk centerline or canopy edge measurements.","reasoning":"Without dimensions annotated on the plan, the measurement reference point cannot be verified. This is a verification issue rather than a documented violation, making it not-verifiable rather than a clear fail.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) - entire drawing where overhead electric facilities and proposed trees are shown"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While both proposed trees (SY, PL, P, M symbols) and overhead electric lines (OHE) are shown together on the landscape plan, clearance verification is prevented by the absence of clearance annotations, dimension lines, and clearance zone notes. Trees are shown in close proximity to the OHE line (measured at 0.4-1.1 feet), but there is no documentation (dimensions, notes, clearance zones marked, or cross-reference to Austin Energy approval) indicating whether this proximity is intentional and approved or an error. The plan must include sufficient documentation to allow verification that proposed tree placement complies with required clearances. Currently, trees near OHE cannot be verified as compliant.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check confirmed that both trees (SY, PL, P, M symbols) and OHE line are visible on Sheet 31, with some trees very close to the line (0.4-1.1 feet per measurement). However, the plan contains no annotations indicating clearance distances, clearance zones, or any documentation explaining how these close placements comply with clearance requirements. No notes refer to Austin Energy approval or exceptions.","reasoning":"Showing both elements on the same plan is necessary but not sufficient. Clearance compliance verification requires documentation (dimensions, zone markings, or approval letters) demonstrating the spatial relationship is intentional and compliant. The absence of this documentation prevents verification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary where proposed trees are located 0.4-1.1 feet from OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Sheet 35 - Landscape Calculations (Plant List)"}],"comment":"Proposed trees (mitigation trees marked 'M') are positioned within prohibited clearance zones: at 0.4-1.1 feet from the OHE distribution line, which violates the 15-foot minimum clearance for any tree and 25-foot minimum for large trees per UCM § 1.10.10.4. The proposed plant list includes large trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak - both 40+ feet mature height) which require 25-foot clearance. No documentation of written approval from Austin Energy authorizing these placements in restricted zones is provided in the site plan documents, supplementary documents reviewed, or any attached correspondence. Plans cannot propose trees in prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy approval.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement shows proposed 'M' trees at 0.4-1.1 feet from OHE line (Sheet 31). Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists Cedar Elm and Live Oak as proposed shade/mitigation trees (large trees, 40+ feet). No letter, approval, email, or other correspondence from Austin Energy appears in the supplementary documents index or site plan notes authorizing this placement.","reasoning":"Trees at 0.4-1.1 feet clearly violate minimum clearance distances (15 feet for any tree, 25 feet for large trees). The regulatory exception allows trees in prohibited zones only with 'explicit written approval from Austin Energy.' No such approval is documented in the site plan submittal.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1786,"cache_read_input_tokens":67401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1786},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c8f4369-ba37-4038-94f5-e0bc36accce4","uuid":"887de08b-b312-436e-b961-bf0179cb83c7"}
