{"level":30,"time":1778516485257,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0147QHmrWkiHExQnmuaUhFTJ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Block 14\n     2→\n     3→## text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion control, and safety clearances. Contains information regarding the developer's responsibility for tree pruning, erosion control, and maintaining clearances according to safety codes.\n     4→\n     5→Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n     6→\n     7→The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n     8→\n     9→The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electrical facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n    10→\n    11→The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n    12→\n    13→Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at landowner's/developer’s expense.\n    14→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02f3e714-877a-4005-af51-2af8f544a8d6","uuid":"b76c6cbc-11a3-46b6-b87f-c9bf10b10f14","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/wip/measure-distance-tool/vv-el-run/2026-04-15/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-14.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Block 14\n\n## text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion control, and safety clearances. Contains information regarding the developer's responsibility for tree pruning, erosion control, and maintaining clearances according to safety codes.\n\nAustin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n\nThe owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n\nThe owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electrical facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n\nThe owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n\nAny relocation of electric facilities shall be at landowner's/developer’s expense.\n","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778516494679,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0129Z13yJqnqEtgKfoVHwHEv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting. Block 14 states: \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment.\"\n\nThis acknowledges the requirement to maintain clearances but doesn't specifically include the 48-hour notification requirement note that the grouping specifies should be on the plans. The requirement EL-1.46 specifically asks for \"plans do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines\" per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.\n\nBlock 14 and Block 8 (same content) acknowledge the need to maintain clearances per NESC and OSHA, but don't include the specific 48-hour notification requirement to Austin Energy before commencing work.\n\nBlock 20 (Electric Transmission Notes) DOES include this for transmission facilities but not for distribution facilities.\n\nNow, the key question is: Are there existing transmission lines or just distribution lines? Let me review the facts and vision checks again...\n\nFrom the vision check on Sheet 31:\n- Overhead electric lines are shown (OHE - Overhead Electric)\n- No designation of whether they are distribution or transmission\n\nFrom the notes:\n- Block 8 says \"overhead and underground electric facilities\" for service to the building\n- Block 14 mentions \"proposed overhead electrical facilities designed to provide electric service to this project\"  \n- Block 20 addresses transmission lines with specific contact info\n- Block 8 mentions a \"center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities\"\n\nWait, \"proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project\"... If this is PROPOSED overhead service, that would be new. But the site plan shows UNDERGROUND service to the buildings on Sheet 21. So the \"proposed overhead electric facilities\" mentioned may be referring to something else, or may be outdated language.\n\n\nThe overhead lines visible on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) and existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) appear to be existing infrastructure rather than new construction. This creates some ambiguity about whether they're distribution or transmission lines. The plans show proposed underground service to buildings on Sheet 21, so the overhead facilities referenced in the notes may be legacy language or refer to something distinct. Key deficiencies remain: no building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor heights, no dimension annotations from building edges to overhead lines, and unclear tree placement relative to overhead facilities.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":923,"cache_read_input_tokens":90541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":923},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02f3e714-877a-4005-af51-2af8f544a8d6","uuid":"fef75525-a7df-4c2a-aa14-173b9fd71d7b"}
{"level":30,"time":1778516495201,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0129Z13yJqnqEtgKfoVHwHEv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review of the site plan documents, let me now systematically evaluate the checklist items. I've gathered sufficient evidence from:\n- The landscape plan (Sheet 31) showing OHE lines along property edges\n- The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) showing utility poles and lines\n- The site plan (Sheet 9) with building locations\n- Electrical notes (Sheet 3, Blocks 8, 14, 20) detailing requirements\n- Plant lists (Sheet 35) showing trees without specific placement mapping near OHE\n\nLet me compile my findings:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":923,"cache_read_input_tokens":90541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":923},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02f3e714-877a-4005-af51-2af8f544a8d6","uuid":"7a0b7cc1-99dc-4ffa-8a87-dc044a3a3c5a"}
{"level":30,"time":1778516513104,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0129Z13yJqnqEtgKfoVHwHEv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GHjqsKp56fPdsug655jDcd","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric utility lines (OHE) are shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) and existing conditions survey (Sheet 4), running along the left (Valley View Road) and southern property edges. Building locations are shown on the site plan (Sheet 9).","reasoning":"While overhead lines are present on the site, no clearance dimensions are annotated between the buildings and these overhead conductors on any sheets reviewed. The presence of overhead lines and buildings in proximity triggers the requirement for documented clearances.","tools_used":["vision"]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Areas along Valley View Road property frontage and southern property edge where OHE lines run"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines shown on landscape plan and existing conditions survey in proximity to buildings, but no clearance dimension annotations provided to verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement is met."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan set includes 39 sheets covering site plans, grading, drainage, utilities, landscape, and construction details. No building elevation sheets or profile views showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations are included in the sheet index or accessed during review.","reasoning":"The grouping requirement specifies that buildings within potential clearance distance of overhead lines require surveyed conductor elevation data on building elevation sheets. The absence of such elevation sheets from the entire 39-sheet set means the required documentation is missing.","tools_used":["vision"]},"status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All building locations near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets showing surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are not included in the site plan set. Vertical clearance cannot be verified without elevation views of the conductors and building features."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) confirmed that while general setback dimensions exist (e.g., '25'' dimensions near buildings), no dimension annotations specifically show clearances from the outer conductor to building edges.","reasoning":"The grouping requires section and plan view exhibits with dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of buildings. Absence of such dimension annotations on both plan view sheets demonstrates the required exhibits are missing.","tools_used":["vision"]},"status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All areas where buildings are within potential clearance distance of overhead conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Dimension exhibits showing clearances from outer electric conductor to building edges are not provided on site plan or landscape plan sheets. Required section and plan view clearance dimensions are missing."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 9 confirmed that while some dimension annotations exist on the site plan (setback dimensions like '25'' and '21.3'''), none are labeled as clearance dimensions to overhead electric conductors, and none indicate measurement points (pole centerline vs. outside conductor).","reasoning":"The requirement specifies that clearance dimensions must originate from the outside conductor, not pole centerline. Since no clearance dimensions to overhead conductors are shown at all, the issue of measurement methodology (pole vs. conductor) cannot be verified, making the deficiency not-verifiable from the current documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All locations where overhead utility poles and conductors are shown relative to structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are provided on the plans that would show whether measurements are taken from pole centerline or outside conductor. Measurement methodology cannot be verified when clearance dimensions are absent."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 31 identified that overhead electric utility lines (OHE) run along the southern property edge, with tree symbols shown within 10 feet of the line. The plant list (Sheet 35) specifies tree species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) but does not provide location-specific mapping indicating which species are planted near the OHE line.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates verification that trees within 10 feet of distribution conductors are utility-compatible species from ECM Appendix F. The landscape plan shows trees near the OHE line but uses generic classification codes (SY, M, PL) without cross-referencing to specific species in proximity to the line. This prevents verification of species compatibility.","tools_used":["vision"]},"status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas adjacent to the OHE line running along the southern property edge"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on the landscape plan within 10 lateral feet of the OHE line, but their specific species are not documented in the landscape plan drawing. Without location-specific tree species identification, compliance with utility-compatible species requirements cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3, Block 20 contains Electric Transmission Notes that include a requirement for 'a pre-construction safety meeting with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction,' which addresses transmission facilities. However, Block 8 (Electric Notes) for distribution facilities acknowledges responsibility for maintaining NESC/OSHA clearances but does not include a specific 48-hour notification requirement note.","reasoning":"The grouping requirement specifies a general note that must appear when overhead electric lines exist and construction is proposed, referencing Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752. While transmission notes address some pre-construction coordination, no blanket notification requirement note is provided for distribution line work.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet or general notes applicable to entire site with overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While transmission facility notes require 48-hour pre-construction safety meetings, no specific owner/contractor notification requirement note per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 is documented for general overhead line work on the plans."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":923,"cache_read_input_tokens":90541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":923},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02f3e714-877a-4005-af51-2af8f544a8d6","uuid":"724ebe65-908f-435e-ac2c-192d7ce77de7"}
