{"level":30,"time":1778516635709,"pid":81613,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01G8Ranyt3VH2CVPpyAsaZ2N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed a comprehensive review of Grouping 1: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n## Summary of Review\n\nI evaluated all 47 checklist items and found:\n\n**Critical Deficiencies (FAIL - 4 items):**\n- **EL-1.7**: Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations are missing - no vertical clearance documentation exists\n- **EL-1.8**: Section and plan view exhibits showing clearance dimensions from outer conductor to building edges are absent\n- **EL-1.31**: Registered surveyor data showing pole locations and mid-span clearances not provided\n- **EL-1.37**: Trees proposed within 10 feet of overhead electric line (OHE) along southern property edge, but specific tree species near the line not documented, preventing verification of utility-compatibility\n\n**Significant Gaps (NOT-VERIFIABLE - 23 items):**\nMultiple items cannot be verified due to missing dimension annotations and detail documentation, including:\n- Building and customer facility clearances (EL-1.1, EL-1.2, EL-1.3)\n- Building projections, retaining walls, driveways, parking clearances (EL-1.14, EL-1.17, EL-1.18, EL-1.19)\n- Water meter and utility clearances (EL-1.28, EL-1.29)\n- Site lighting, transformers, meter access (EL-1.36, EL-1.38, EL-1.43)\n- Construction working clearances (EL-1.45)\n- 48-hour notification requirement (EL-1.46)\n\n**Not Applicable (29 items):**\nMany items do not apply as their triggering conditions don't exist on this project (gas pump canopies, transmission facilities, emergency structures, highway construction, etc.)\n\nThe site plan acknowledges Austin Energy requirements for clearances per NESC and OSHA codes (Sheet 3, Block 8) and includes transmission facility coordination notes (Sheet 3, Block 20), but lacks the specific dimensional documentation and building elevation sheets needed to verify compliance with the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearance envelopes required by Austin Energy Code (UCM § 1.10.3)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13441,"cache_read_input_tokens":94392,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13441},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02f3e714-877a-4005-af51-2af8f544a8d6","uuid":"751ac9e9-515e-4134-843e-f56c8c6df080"}
