":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All building projections proposed on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building projection details and clearances from overhead conductors are not documented. Building elevation sheets required to verify clearance compliance are not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review reveals no gas pump canopies or fuel service areas proposed on the site. The project is a multi-family residential development without commercial fuel service.","reasoning":"Gas pump canopies are not shown anywhere on the site plan. The triggering condition (gas pump canopies proposed) does not exist for this project.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Gas pump canopies are not proposed as part of this multi-family residential development. Requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows internal pedestrian walkways and driveways but no elevated stairs, elevated walkways, or elevated platforms as distinct structures proposed as part of new construction.","reasoning":"The applicability condition specifies elevated walkways and platforms. The proposed concrete and decomposed granite walkways appear to be ground-level, not elevated structures.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No elevated walkways or elevated platforms proposed. Requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","agentTrace":{"observation":"Buildings are shown with approximate 25-30 foot setbacks from property lines based on site plan. Valley View Road ROW likely contains the documented OHE lines shown on landscape plan.","reasoning":"Buildings appear separated from property line by developed area. However, without specific ROW boundary information and conductor elevation data, compliance with both clearance envelopes (7.5-foot and 15-foot) cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings in relation to potential overhead electric facilities in adjacent ROW"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance verification from buildings to electric facilities in adjacent right-of-way cannot be completed without explicit dimension annotations and surveyed conductor location data."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","agentTrace":{"observation":"Complete site plan set of 39 sheets reviewed. No building elevation sheets or profile sections showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations and locations are included. All sheets focus on plan views, details, and supporting documentation.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors on building elevation sheets for structures within clearance distance. The systematic absence of building elevation sheets from the entire drawing set means this required documentation class is not provided.","tools_used":[]},"status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All building locations within potential overhead conductor clearance distance"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations are not included in the site plan set. Vertical clearance verification requires elevation documentation that is absent."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision inspection of site plan (Sheet 9) and landscape plan (Sheet 31) confirmed that dimension annotations show general setbacks but no specific dimension lines originating from outer electric conductor to building edges or projections.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates section and plan view exhibits with dimensions showing clearance from outer conductor to outermost building edge. Absence of such dimension lines in both primary view sheets indicates required exhibits are missing.","tools_used":["vision"]},"status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All areas where buildings and structures are within potential conductor clearance distance"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits showing clearance dimensions from outer electric conductor to building edges are not provided. Required dimensional documentation is missing from all reviewed sheets."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fences are indicated on existing conditions survey Sheet 4 (chain link, wood, wire, crete fences shown in legend and on drawing). No fences appear to be proposed as new structures on the site plan per the landscape/site plan sheets.","reasoning":"The applicability condition requires new fences proposed and overhead facilities to exist. While overhead lines are shown, no clear indication of proposed new fencing requiring clearance verification is documented.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new fence construction is clearly proposed on the site plan. Existing fences are shown but requirement applies to proposed fences. Condition does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows utility pole symbols. However, the site plan and landscape plan do not appear to show proposed new fences with post locations dimensioned relative to existing poles.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies fence posts maintaining 10-foot clearance from electric poles. No proposed fence structure with documented post locations is visible on the plans being reviewed.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No proposed fence construction with documented post locations relative to existing poles is shown. Requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site facts and plans review reveals no Austin Energy substation on or immediately adjacent to the property. Fences near substation do not apply.","reasoning":"The applicability condition explicitly requires fences adjacent to or connecting with existing Austin Energy substation fences. No substation infrastructure is documented on this site.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation exists on or adjacent to property. Substation isolation fence requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site is located in urban Austin area with existing overhead utility lines (OHE) shown. These appear to be distribution-level lines based on context (residential area, moderate-height poles). No explicit transmission line structures (large towers, high-voltage designation 60kV+) are documented.","reasoning":"Requirement applies to transmission lines (≥60kV) only. Without clear documentation of transmission facilities or evidence of high-voltage transmission presence, the applicability cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fencing near electric transmission lines requirement applies only to transmission voltage (≥60kV). Plans do not clearly document transmission facilities on site."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan does not show vehicle barrier fencing or barrier posts beneath or adjacent to overhead electric lines. Trash enclosures and bollards are shown but not specifically characterized as vehicle barriers.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies vehicle barrier posts or fencing beneath or adjacent to overhead lines. No such structures are clearly documented as proposed.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle barrier fencing or posts beneath overhead lines are shown as proposed. Requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining walls are shown on site plan (Sheet 9) and exist around site perimeter and within site areas. Overhead electric lines (OHE) are shown on landscape plan along property edges. Proximity relationship exists but no clearance dimensions are provided.","reasoning":"Retaining walls are proposed and overhead facilities exist. The requirement mandates 7.5-foot clearance. No dimension annotations from outer electric line to wall face are provided to verify compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All retaining walls in proximity to OHE lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are proposed near overhead lines, but clearance dimension annotations are not provided. Compliance with 7.5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site facts review confirms no Austin Energy substation exists on adjacent property. Retaining wall separation requirements for substations do not apply.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when retaining walls are adjacent to Austin Energy substation property. No substation is documented.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation adjacent to property. Substation wall separation requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows no dedicated emergency access bridges or elevated platform structures distinct from building or pedestrian infrastructure.","reasoning":"The applicability condition requires emergency access structures such as bridges or elevated platforms. Standard building construction and ground-level walkways do not constitute emergency access structures as contemplated by the requirement.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dedicated emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms) are proposed. Requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining wall sections are shown on Wall Plan sheets (Sheets 38-39) but do not include dimension lines showing clearance from electric conductors to wall outer edges.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates section exhibits showing clearance dimensions from outer conductor to outermost wall edge. No such dimension annotations are present on the wall section sheets.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All retaining wall sections in proximity to overhead conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining wall section exhibits are provided but do not include clearance dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to wall face."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows internal driveways throughout the site. Grading plan and utility plans show finished grade information. However, no sections or profiles showing vertical clearance dimensions between driveway grades and overhead conductor clearance envelopes are provided.","reasoning":"Driveways are proposed and overhead lines exist. The requirement mandates clearance verification for driveways (16 feet for non-truck areas, 18 feet for truck traffic). No vertical clearance dimension exhibits document this. Without determination of truck traffic use and vertical clearance profiles, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["All internal driveways on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways are shown on site plan with grading information, but no vertical clearance profiles or dimensions from driveway surface to overhead conductors are provided. Clearance compliance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows parking garage structures and surface parking areas. However, no specific dimensions or notes documenting vertical clearance from parked vehicle height to lowest overhead electric line are provided.","reasoning":"Parking exists but no clearance dimension annotations address the specific requirement for parking areas under overhead lines. Required documentation is absent.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Parking areas (surface and garage) on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Parking areas exist but vertical clearance dimensions from parking surfaces to overhead lines are not provided. Requirement verification documents are absent."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","agentTrace":{"observation":"No roads or driveways are documented as being beneath or under electric transmission line structures. Transmission facilities are not clearly documented as existing on site.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only to roads beneath transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV). Without clear transmission facility documentation, applicability cannot be established.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No roads or driveways documented as beneath transmission lines. Transmission infrastructure not confirmed on site."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","agentTrace":{"observation":"No highway or freeway construction is proposed. Requirement applies to highway/freeway grading with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures.","reasoning":"Highway/freeway is not part of this site plan project scope. Applicability condition not met.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No highway or freeway grading proposed. Requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows utility pole locations. Driveways are proposed on site plan. However, no specific conflict between existing poles and proposed driveway alignments is documented or flagged, and no relocation notes appear on the plans.","reasoning":"The applicability condition requires proposed driveways shown in conflict with or immediately adjacent to existing poles. If such conflicts exist, relocation must be 30 feet minimum or notes provided. No such documentation is apparent.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Driveway alignments relative to existing pole locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Relationship between driveway locations and existing electric poles not clearly documented with conflict resolution or relocation notes where applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check confirmed that while general property line and building setback dimensions exist on site plans, no dimensions specifically show clearance from electric poles or conductors. Therefore, methodology for measuring (pole center vs. outside conductor) cannot be evaluated.","reasoning":"The requirement addresses measurement methodology only in the context of clearance dimensions being shown. Since no clearance dimensions are present, methodology cannot be assessed. The deficiency is actually that dimensions are missing entirely.","tools_used":["vision"]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Any locations where overhead electric infrastructure is shown"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are present on plans that would reveal whether measurements are from pole centerline or outside conductor. Methodology cannot be verified because required dimensions are absent."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) legend identifies 'light pole' symbol. Landscape plan and site plan do not appear to show new streetlight pole locations beneath overhead line routing.","reasoning":"The applicability condition requires new streetlight poles proposed and overhead lines existing. No new streetlight poles clearly documented as proposed in conflict with overhead lines.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"New streetlight poles under overhead lines are not clearly documented as proposed. Requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sidewalks are shown on site plan along property frontage (Valley View Road side). Existing conditions survey shows power poles exist near the property. However, no specific clearance dimensions from sidewalk edges to pole centers are documented.","reasoning":"Requirement applies when new/modified sidewalks intersect existing pole locations at property ends along ROW. Visual evidence suggests this may occur but clearance documentation is not provided.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalk alignments at property frontage extremities where power poles may exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalk-to-pole clearance relationship at property ends not documented with specific dimensions. Verification cannot be completed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows trash enclosure areas but does not document specific locations relative to overhead conductors or clearance heights for raised trash receptacles.","reasoning":"Trash enclosures are shown but their proximity to overhead lines and clearance verification during bin service (when bins are elevated) are not documented.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash enclosure locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trash enclosure placement relative to overhead facilities and clearance for raised bins not documented with dimension annotations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows all proposed improvements. No structures are visibly located directly beneath the documented OHE lines. However, no explicit certification or dimension showing that structures maintain required separation from overhead distribution facilities is provided.","reasoning":"The absolute prohibition against customer facilities under or over distribution lines requires affirmative documentation that this prohibition is met. Absence of such documentation creates a verification gap.","tools_used":["vision"]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings and structures in relation to overhead distribution lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No explicit clearance verification or dimensional proof that structures are not placed under/over distribution facilities. Affirmative compliance documentation is absent."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","agentTrace":{"observation":"Water service infrastructure is shown on utility plan (Sheet 19-20) with meter locations indicated. However, specific clearance dimension annotations from overhead service drop conductors to water meters are not provided.","reasoning":"Requirement applies when water meters exist and overhead service drops are present. Service-drop conductors and meter locations are not dimensionally verified for required 7.5-foot clearance.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meter clearance from overhead service drop conductors not documented with specific dimension annotations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","agentTrace":{"observation":"Water lines are shown on utility plan. Overhead utility lines (OHE) are documented on landscape and existing conditions surveys. However, no specific clearance dimensions between water line routing and overhead electric poles/conductors are provided.","reasoning":"New water lines are shown and overhead distribution facilities exist. Clearance documentation showing minimum separation is absent.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water line routing in relation to overhead electric infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water line clearance from overhead electric distribution facilities not documented. Coordination of utility routing not demonstrated."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building foundations within typical setbacks from property line. Sheet 3 notes indicate 'Additional electric easements may be required at a later date' but no baseline electric facility spacing requirement is documented.","reasoning":"Requirement applies when permanent foundations are within 5 feet of property line and electric facilities exist or are planned in adjacent ROW/property. General situation exists but specific foundation-to-property-line-to-facility clearances not documented.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Building foundations in proximity to property lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Foundation clearance space for electric facilities not explicitly documented. Required spacing for utility access not verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","agentTrace":{"observation":"No registered surveyor's report showing pole locations and mid-span clearances is included in the site plan set. Vertical clearance verification from overhead lines to buildings/driveways relies on estimated heights without surveyed data.","reasoning":"When vertical clearance appears marginal, registered surveyor data is required. The apparent proximity of buildings to overhead lines without clearance dimensions suggests this requirement should apply, but the data is absent.","tools_used":[]},"status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All areas where proposed site features may have marginal vertical clearance from overhead facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Survey by registered surveyor showing pole locations and mid-span conductor clearances not provided. Vertical clearance verification by surveyed data is absent when needed to demonstrate marginal clearance adequacy."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","agentTrace":{"observation":"No new overhead electric lines are proposed to be constructed as part of this site plan. The project shows proposed underground service and connection to existing overhead service points.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only when new overhead electric lines are being constructed and they cross proposed roadways. This condition does not exist on this site plan.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new overhead electric lines are proposed to cross roadways. Requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows proposed underground service. Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows overhead utility lines. No configuration detail showing secondary lines crossing over primary lines is documented.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only when both secondary and primary overhead lines are shown in site routing configuration. No detailed overhead line crossing documentation exists.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No documented secondary and primary overhead line crossing configuration shown. Requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","agentTrace":{"observation":"No marquee signs are shown on the site plan. The project is multi-family residential without marquee signage.","reasoning":"Marquee signs are not proposed. Applicability condition not met.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Marquee signs are not proposed on site. Requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site shows proposed underground electrical service. Existing poles are shown on existing conditions survey. However, no notes document installation of new poles for underground service conversion or spacing of such new poles from existing poles.","reasoning":"The requirement applies when new poles are proposed for underground service conversion. No new pole locations are explicitly documented as proposed, making applicability unclear.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"New power poles for underground service conversion not clearly shown as proposed on site plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows proposed site lighting. However, specific lighting fixture locations relative to overhead electric line routing and clearance verification are not dimensioned.","reasoning":"Decorative and site lighting exist but clearance compliance with overhead lines is not documented through dimension annotations.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed decorative and site lighting locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Decorative lighting location clearances from overhead lines not documented with dimension annotations. Relocation or clearance verification not shown."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of landscape plan (Sheet 31) confirmed trees are shown within 10 feet of the OHE line along the southern property edge. Plant list (Sheet 35) specifies tree species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) but the landscape plan uses generic classification codes (SY, M, PL) without mapping specific species to locations near the OHE line.","reasoning":"Trees are proposed within 10 feet of distribution conductors. The requirement mandates verification that trees are utility-compatible species per ECM Appendix F. The landscape plan shows trees near OHE but does not identify specific species in that area, preventing verification of species compatibility. This constitutes a failure to document compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas within 10 feet of OHE line along southern property edge"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are proposed within 10 feet of overhead distribution conductors, but specific species identification at those locations is not provided on the landscape plan. Utility-compatibility of trees in the OHE proximity zone cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","agentTrace":{"observation":"Meter locations are shown on utility plan. Site plan shows building locations and access ways. However, specific analysis of meter access obstructions is not documented. No detailed meter area plan showing 30-inch-wide front space and 36-inch depth access is provided.","reasoning":"Meters are proposed. The requirement mandates unobstructed access space. No detailed meter enclosure plan demonstrating compliance or identifying obstructions is provided.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["All meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Meter access obstructions not analyzed. Detailed meter installation plan showing required clearances not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","agentTrace":{"observation":"New buildings are proposed. Existing streetlight pole locations would be shown in existing conditions survey (Sheet 4 shows 'light pole' in legend but specific locations require visual inspection of drawing). No explicit clearance analysis between proposed buildings and streetlight poles is documented.","reasoning":"Buildings are proposed adjacent to existing streetlight infrastructure. Clearance verification between structures and these utility poles is not documented.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings in relation to existing streetlight pole locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building clearances from existing streetlight poles not documented with specific dimensions."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) legend includes utility pole symbols. Down guy wires would be shown with poles if present but are not explicitly called out in available block descriptions. Driveways and accessible paths are proposed on site plan.","reasoning":"Applicability requires documented down guy wire conflicts with accessible paths/driveways. No explicit down guy documentation appears in reviewed materials, so applicability is unclear.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy wires from existing poles not documented on plans or not in conflict with proposed features. Condition does not clearly apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","agentTrace":{"observation":"If transmission facilities exist on site (unclear from available documentation), angled guy anchors would require dedicated easements per the requirement. However, transmission facility presence is not confirmed, and transmission vs. distribution distinction not made explicit.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only to transmission facility guy wires. Applicability depends on confirmed transmission presence, which is not clearly documented for this site.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission facility guy wire easements require documentation only if transmission lines confirmed present. Site transmission status unclear."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","agentTrace":{"observation":"Down guy anchors from distribution poles (if present) would require dedicated easements. However, no down guy infrastructure is explicitly shown on reviewed site plans or utility documentation.","reasoning":"Requirement applies when down guy anchors exist and require easements. No down guy documentation is apparent in the site plan set.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy anchor easements required only if down guys documented. No down guy infrastructure shown on plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformers as part of proposed electric infrastructure. Sheet shows 'transformer on pad' in legend of existing conditions survey. However, no section views showing vertical clearance from overhead lines to transformer tops are provided.","reasoning":"Transformers are shown but no section view dimensions demonstrating 7.5-foot vertical clearance from overhead lines to transformer equipment are documented.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer vertical clearance from overhead lines not documented with section view dimensions."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transformers are shown on electrical design plan as pad-mounted equipment. No niche enclosure configurations (with overhead structures/canopies) are documented.","reasoning":"The 35-foot clearance requirement applies only to transformer/switchgear niche configurations with covered/recessed installations. Standard pad-mounted transformers do not trigger this requirement.","tools_used":[]},"status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche-configured transformer/switchgear installations shown. Niche clearance requirement does not apply."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site has existing overhead electric facilities. Construction staging, equipment lay-down, and work platform areas are referenced in general construction notes but no detailed construction logistics plan showing staging area clearances from overhead lines is provided.","reasoning":"Construction activities are proposed near overhead facilities. OSHA 10-foot radial working clearance requirement should be documented on construction logistics plan, but such plan detail or clearance notes are not provided in available documentation.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging and work areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Construction staging areas and equipment work zones not documented with 10-foot radial clearance dimensions from energized overhead lines. Construction logistics plan details lacking."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3, Block 8 (Electric Notes) addresses owner responsibility for maintaining clearances per NESC/OSHA/City codes/Texas law. Sheet 3, Block 20 (Electric Transmission Notes) requires 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting for transmission facilities. However, a general blanket note applying to all overhead electric line work citing Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 is not explicitly documented.","reasoning":"Block 8 acknowledges clearance maintenance requirements but does not include specific 48-hour notification requirement. Block 20 addresses transmission facilities specifically. A general note applying to distribution line work appears to be missing.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet or general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Specific 48-hour notification requirement note per Texas Health & Safety Code not documented on plans. Transmission-specific meeting requirement noted but general overhead line notification requirement not explicitly stated."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and building elevations not reviewed in detail. Service-mast through-roof installations are not prominently documented in available plan excerpts.","reasoning":"Service-mast roof penetrations would appear on building elevations. Since building elevation sheets are not included in the site plan set, service-mast details and roof clearances cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Service-mast roof installations if proposed"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Service-mast through-roof clearances cannot be verified without building elevation sheets showing roof penetration details and clearance dimensions."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7ca9379b-43f7-41ab-95d5-a4421e9977b0"}
